From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 00:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] waydroid-luneos: do not re-show a full UI that is already up

Every launch of the LuneOS entry added a card, and none of them could be
dismissed.

The session starts Android with waydroid.background_start=true, and the
hwcomposer sets waydroid.active_apps=Waydroid while it initialises, so the
full-UI window exists and is already a card before anyone taps the launcher.
Calling show-full-ui again is not idempotent: showFullUI() ends with a
"refresh display contents" step - settingsPutString(policy_control) plus a
status bar expand/collapse - and that makes the hwcomposer tear down its window
and create a new one.

The replacement surface is mapped as a fresh card, but the old surface is never
destroyed or unmapped, so it stays on screen as a live second card with nothing
behind it. Waydroid itself reports waydroid.open_windows=1 throughout, which is
why nothing on the Android side looks wrong.

Measured on mindphone from a clean boot, counting onSurfaceMapped for the
Waydroid appId in the compositor:

  session autostart only .................. 1 mapped surface, 1 card
  after one launch of id.waydro.container .. 2 mapped surfaces, 2 cards

and stopping the session removed both, confirming both belonged to it.

webOS is unusually exposed to this. A mapped surface that sets no window type
defaults to _WEBOS_WINDOW_TYPE_CARD - deliberately, so that plain Qt apps get a
card - so a leaked surface is not merely invisible clutter, it is a card.

Skip the call when the UI is already showing; the card exists and the shell
brings it forward by itself.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific launcher]
---
--- a/data/scripts/waydroid-luneos.sh
+++ b/data/scripts/waydroid-luneos.sh
@@ -1,3 +1,24 @@
 #!/bin/sh
+# LuneOS launcher entry for the Android full UI.
+#
+# Only ask for the full UI when the session is not already running.
+#
+# The session starts Android with waydroid.background_start=true and the
+# hwcomposer sets waydroid.active_apps=Waydroid as it initialises, so once the
+# session is up the full-UI window already exists and is already a card.
+# Calling show-full-ui again is not idempotent: it ends with a "refresh display
+# contents" step - policy_control plus a status bar expand/collapse - which
+# makes the hwcomposer tear down its window and build a new one. The
+# replacement is mapped as another card while the old surface is never
+# unmapped, so every launch leaves behind a card nothing can dismiss.
+#
+# Test with "waydroid status" rather than the active_apps property: SAM runs
+# this script without the session user's DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS, and
+# "waydroid prop get" needs it - without it the command answers "WayDroid
+# session is stopped" no matter what is on screen. "waydroid status" talks to
+# the container service on the system bus and works either way.
+if /usr/bin/waydroid status 2>/dev/null | grep -q "^Session:.*RUNNING"; then
+    exit 0
+fi
 
-/usr/bin/waydroid show-full-ui
\ No newline at end of file
+exec /usr/bin/waydroid show-full-ui
